    {
      "id": "4ae32fb5-78e1-4bf9-824b-b38c7463f685",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2240,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 656,
        "height": 608,
        "content": "## Data Ingestion & Triage\n\nThis phase initiates the audit. It pulls specific client details from Salesforce—such as Name and Tier—and uses a Switch node to route the workflow. It separates Platinum clients who haven't been contacted from those who already have \"Alert\" statuses in their description."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ce5cfdd1-8047-408d-acc6-25e0145a2c3b",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1504,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 816,
        "height": 608,
        "content": "## AI Strategy & Task Creation\n\nHere, the workflow uses Groq LLMs to \"think.\" For neglected clients, it creates a \"Rescue Task\" in Salesforce and alerts the team via Slack. For over-saturated clients, it skips task creation and instead provides a \"Cool-down\" strategy via Slack to prevent intrusive communication."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4cbeb19c-0a5e-41cf-a918-aa6047eca8e6",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -608,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 688,
        "height": 608,
        "content": "## The 24h Accountability Loop\n\nThis is the verification stage. The workflow pauses for 24 hours to give the team time to act. Once the wait is over, it re-queries Salesforce to check the status of the specific \"Rescue Task\" to see if it has been moved to \"Completed.\""
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "8167eb8f-68eb-4432-ae92-e8fa2d95b0fc",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        208,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 960,
        "height": 992,
        "content": "## Reporting & Final Logging\n\nThe final phase handles the outcome. If the task was completed, it sends a success message; if not, it triggers an urgent management escalation on Slack. Finally, it updates the Salesforce Account description with a timestamped audit result to keep a permanent record."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1290bedc-e8ec-4791-a31f-fd07c21a077c",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -3152,
        -112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 816,
        "height": 816,
        "content": "## Customer Communication Load Balancer\n\n## How it works\nThis workflow acts as an automated triage for your high-value clients. It pulls account data from Salesforce and uses logic to determine if a Platinum partner is being \"Neglected\" (no recent activity) or is \"Over-Saturated\" (too many recent alerts). Depending on the state, Groq-powered AI agents generate either a high-priority rescue strategy or a low-touch \"cool-down\" plan. For neglected VIPs, the system creates a Salesforce task and triggers a 24-hour audit loop to ensure the team follows through.\n\n## Setup steps\n\n1. Connect Salesforce, Slack, and Groq API credentials.\n2. In SF: Fetch Account Data, replace the Account ID with the client you want to audit.\n3. Update all Slack nodes with your Slack User ID to receive alerts.\n4. Make sure Salesforce has:\n    Customer_Tier__c\n    Description\n5. Change the 24h Wait node if you want faster testing.\n6. Run once, test both branches, then activate workflow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
